   200	(`CH:373`); DETECTOR-NULL gives `δ⁰ ≥ 1` on every minor branch; the covering is
   201	exhaustive (`CH:685-688`: "every subdisc of a tower disc is major … or minor
   202	(Prop 6.1), and a tower halting above level 1 leaves its roots in minor discs,
   203	contributing 0"). Hence
   204	
   205	```text
   206	 {D branches of a generic fibre} = PROPER (bottom-major discs) ⊔ NON-PROPER (minor discs)
   207	 N = sum over the PROPER block only;   the NON-PROPER block contributes exactly 0.
   208	```
