+## 4. Q4 -- Software Program
+
+Build `globalinterp` in the smallest useful version this week:
+
+```text
+Input:
+  one (1)-(13) skeleton, chosen branch multiset/k, target N, and a truncation order.
+
+Core:
+  1. Construct the bottom STAR-ABC normal form for each bottom disc.
+  2. Declare the exponent semigroup and separate inner unknown coefficients from
+     prescribed outer/minor contributions.
+  3. For every root tau_i of g-c_2, compute the series for 1/g_y(x,tau_i)
+     to the requested order, integrate formally, and attach a branch constant.
+  4. Build the Lagrange interpolant in y across all n roots symbolically or in
+     a Galois-character-compressed basis.
+  5. Emit the high-y coefficient equations y^70..y^104 and the no-negative-x
+     polynomiality equations order by order.
+  6. Optionally pass through Moh's Prop. 6.3/6.4 approximate-root transform and
+     replace the constant Jacobian by the monomial-Jacobian normal form.
+
+Output:
+  typed rank/cokernel counts per skeleton:
+  unknowns, equations, rank, forced compatibility equations, and whether the
+  pass is local, global-formal, or polynomial.
+```
+
+Gates:
+
+* Positive controls: automorphisms in `box/exactn-drivers-20260902` and the
+  simple `(y,x^j+y^k)` family must pass with the exact interpolant.
+* Negative controls: the seven non-Keller two-tower rows must fail the same
+  global criterion; Moh's `(15,10,M_2=11,V_2=3)` Appendix-II transformed row
+  must reproduce the degree contradiction visible on p.211.
+* Fail-closed ring checks: coefficient field, generator order, quotient/local
+  ring, exponent semigroup, and image maps must be printed in the report. No
+  name-matching `sat()` wrapper.
+* Preflight: any realisation job at `N>=6` consumes `box/preflight.py` first,
+  per `COORDINATION.md:721-723`.
+
+Smallest decisive experiment: group C at `D=105`, `N=9`, `k=17`, first global
+order. It is a one-condition-overdetermined rank test (`34` local bottom
+unknowns against `35` high-y equations before shared variables). If it kills,
+run B and A. If it passes by one exact rank dependency, immediately attempt a
+mod-`p` lift of group A at `N=12`, because that is the first nearby case where
+the count predicts enough freedom for a formal survivor.
